+- **Parallel voter dispatch.** Before a window, re-probe if any probe is 60 minutes old or more; assign every voter in least-recently-used order and write all seat-use lines with the proposal in one window commit; then launch all voters at once, each in its own fresh context through the decision-seat gate. D171 cites stay; re-asks run as a second parallel batch. No commit while a voter runs, for seats as well as the facilitator. If the shared seat-use history cannot be written safely, the window falls back to serial launch and is recorded as a fallback. A window starts only after a preflight, a line of the D158 checklist: the vote prompt is the committed template `.mob/records/templates/vote-prompt.md` (it carries the reply format and the CITE line; no hand-set variable), no other decision run is active and the repository root holds no stray `prompt-*.txt`, the fallback chains name no driver whose probe is out of quota, and a Ready draft or any prompt that is not a vote is never sent through the vote wrapper (it goes to a reply-only seat directly). While bug 365 (the seat-use history race) or bug 374 (stray prompt files) is open, the window runs one seat at a time and the record says so.
+  - Hypothesis: dispatching voters in parallel cuts the minutes per vote window, and a preflight keeps the harness from losing whole windows. Metric: median minutes per vote window, 5 or fewer; and vote windows lost to the harness per card (card 203: 3, about 75 minutes), target 0. Counter-metric: minutes from the committed proposal to the counted window. Trial: 3 vote windows (extended at the card 299 retro), and for the preflight the next 3 cards, counted from Decider D228. Decider D174, started 2026-11-01; tuned by D228.
